<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75043" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρθρ-ινός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">,
			ʽὄρθροσ̓</span> later form (<i><span class="en">
			Phryn.
			<u>PS</u>
			p.93
		</span></i>
		<i><span class="en">
			B.
		</span></i>) for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρθριος,</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			LXX
			<u>Wi.</u>
			11.22
		</span></i>, al. ; <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρθρινὸς οἴχεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					5.176
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Mel.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀ. δῶρα</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				7.195
			</span></i> (Id.) : neut. pl. as Adv., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρθρινὰ παίζειν</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				12.47
			</span></i> (Id.). [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				5.176
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				12.47
			</span></i>, as in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠρινός, θερινός,
			χειμερινός</span>: <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				948
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.160
			</span></i> (Antip. Sid.), etc. make <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ι</span> long,
			prob. in imitation of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπωρῑνῷ</span>
			which is a metr. necessity in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, v. sub voc.]</div>
